<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coutances</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cosedia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Coutances is a town in the Cotentin peninsula of Normandy, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In Roman times, as Cosedia, it became the chief town of the Gallic Unelli, and it was renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salamis-cyprus">Constantia</a> in late antiquity, a name that also gave the Cotentin its name. It has been the seat of a bishopric since the late 5th century, and its Gothic cathedral is one of the finest in Normandy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coutances.jpg" alt="Coutances" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aroche · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coutances_vue_nord.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
